{"ts":"2026-07-30T11:12:41.555Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"4f0b476f130948714074f357","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"}},"op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-30T11:12:41.555Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"The spec claimed 'pm vcs items over a range equals the set pm-changelog independently derives for it'. That claim is WRONG and the check that was supposed to confirm it is what disproved it. pm-changelog answers which items belong in a release's notes and lists completed work; pm vcs items answers which items the commits touched and is status-blind. The changelog's set is therefore a SUBSET. Measured on pm-web's real v2026.07.29..v2026.07.30 range: changelog 2 items {sqg5, dlbe}, pm vcs items 4 {9ulj, dlbe, sqg5, ulgy} — the extra two being OPEN items touched but not finished. The subset relation, not equality, is the correct invariant, and it is now pinned by a test and stated in the README."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-30T11:12:41.555Z"}],"before_hash":"d257c367114a93622f149be653ec3ae803dc204d284adf25b2b1e4f77fe3941b","after_hash":"92c08814cc31d82899dd6b7bf89d7be19e5ec8423b352f5c22b5f95fe6aeeb13"}
